{"content":"Now I have a complete picture of the backend markdown architecture.\n\nh13.\n\n**impl — construction — holders**\n\n- **`markdown.service`** (`internal/markdown/markdown.go:58`) — the sole concrete implementation of the `markdown.Service` interface (`internal/markdown/markdown.go:31`). It wraps a `goldmark.Markdown` instance and satisfies `RenderMarkdown`, `RenderHTML`, `ExtractTags`, `ExtractProperties`, `ExtractAll`, `GenerateSnippet`, `RenameTag`, `ValidateContent`. `RenderMarkdown` in turn delegates to `renderer.MarkdownRenderer` (`internal/markdown/renderer/markdown_renderer.go:15`), built via `renderer.NewMarkdownRenderer()` at `internal/markdown/markdown.go:250`, so that's a secondary concrete piece invoked per-call, not injected.\n\n- **Construction**: `markdown.NewService(opts ...Option)` (`internal/markdown/markdown.go:85`) is the only constructor; it always returns `\u0026service{md: md}` — the interface's factory hides the concrete type. It is called at:\n  - `server/router/api/v1/v1.go:48` inside `NewAPIV1Service`, with `WithTagExtension()` and `WithMentionExtension()` options — this is the production wiring used from `server/server.go:76`.\n  - `server/router/api/v1/test/test_helper.go:44` in test scaffolding (`NewTestService`).\n  - Also directly in `server/router/fileserver/fileserver_test.go:427` and `server/router/rss/rss_test.go:54` for test setups.\n\n- **Holders of the interface** (fields typed `markdown.Service`, not the concrete struct):\n  - `v1.APIV1Service.MarkdownService` (`server/router/api/v1/v1.go:35`) — the interface value created once in `NewAPIV1Service` and reused across the server.\n  - `rss.RSSService.MarkdownService` (`server/router/rss/rss.go:45`) — received via `NewRSSService(...)` at `server/router/rss/rss.go:58`; in production it's handed `apiV1Service.MarkdownService` at `server/server.go:85`, so RSS reuses the same instance rather than constructing its own.\n  - `memopayload.Runner.MarkdownService` (`server/runn